{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:88421",
  "title": "Important: qemu-kvm security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-23 06:45:29"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-24 19:12:26"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Kernel-based Virtual Machine (KVM) is a full virtualization solution for Linux on a variety of architectures. The qemu-kvm packages provide the user-space component for running virtual machines that use KVM.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* qemu-kvm: qemu-guest-agent: Local privilege escalation via symlink attack in guest-ssh-add-authorized-keys (CVE-2026-12080)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* qemu-img can't create a qcow2 overlay with 'data_file' feature on top of a file without destroying the original image [rhel-9.8.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-164549)\n\n* live migration of a VM with a scsi3pr to a node that previously held a reservation on that disk fails. [rhel-9.8.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-280223)\n\n* Fix pending QEMU issues for L1VH GA - QEMU [rhel-9.8.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-283121)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
